    "https://holycross.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester-MA/Data-and-Systems-Coordinator_JREQ-000667": {
      "title": "Data and Systems Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Holy Cross, we are focused on creating a world-class workforce by attracting and retaining employees dedicated to fostering a culture of professionalism, pride, mutual trust, and respect—one that values appreciation and recognition, empowering each of us to flourish both individually and collectively. We seek candidates who are inspired by our mission and values, and who are eager to make a meaningful difference on our campus. Learn more about Life at Holy Cross here. The Registrar's Office seeks a detail-oriented and collaborative Temporary Data and Systems Coordinator to provide critical support for the office's data management, reporting, and student information system operations during a two-year appointment. Working closely with the Data and Systems Manager, this position will help ensure the accuracy, integrity, and effective use of student records and administrative systems while supporting day-to-day operational needs. The successful candidate will assist with data requests, system maintenance, troubleshooting, and data quality initiatives that support the Registrar's Office and the broader campus community. Job Description Major Areas of Responsibility   Data Management and Reporting Assist with responding to routine and ad hoc data requests from campus partners. Support data extraction, validation, and reporting activities. Review and verify data accuracy and consistency across systems. Assist with data audits and data cleanup projects to improve data integrity and reliability.   Systems Support Assist in the day-to-day management and monitoring of the student information system and related applications. Monitor system processes and workflows to ensure scheduled jobs, integrations, and business processes are functioning as expected. Identify, document, and troubleshoot system issues, escalating complex problems as appropriate. Support testing and implementation of system updates, enhancements, and process improvements.   Operational Support Collaborate with Registrar's Office staff to support registration, records management, degree audit, and other key operational functions. Maintain process documentation and assist with developing user guides and training materials. Provide support for special projects and initiatives related to student records, data governance, and systems optimization. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience working with databases, administrative systems, or student information systems preferred. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work with large datasets while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Experience using spreadsheet and reporting tools. Strong communication and customer service skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work collaboratively across departments.   Additional Information: This position works closely with the Registrar's Office staff, academic departments, and other offices across the college. ​ This is a full-time, temporary two-year position designed to support continuity of operations during the implementation of a new Student Information System. The position works closely with Registrar's Office staff, academic departments, students, faculty, and external partner institutions. The hourly range for this position is $30.00 - $33.00/hour. Disclaimer: This description contains the major areas of responsibility and may include other duties as assigned. Weekly Hours: 40 Annual Work Schedule: 52 week (For Seasonal and Temporary Positions, this will be determined by the manager) Application Instructions For all administrative and academic positions, please upload a current resume and cover letter. In your cover letter, please reflect on how your professional and personal values align with the Mission of the College. For all other positions, resume and cover letters are optional, but your most up-to-date work experience and educational background are required. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, priority consideration will be given to applications submitted within 30 days of the posting date. Additional Information To review our generous benefits options, please review our detailed information here or check out our Benefits at a Glance . The College also provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities during the hiring process in compliance with law. Please contact Human Resources for questions or to request an accommodation via email at hr@holycross.edu, or by calling 508-793-3391.  The College is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and complies with all Federal and Massachusetts laws concerning Equal Opportunity in the workplace."
    },
    "https://holycross.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester-MA/Records-and-Registration-Coordinator_JREQ-000668": {
      "title": "Records and Registration Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Holy Cross, we are focused on creating a world-class workforce by attracting and retaining employees dedicated to fostering a culture of professionalism, pride, mutual trust, and respect—one that values appreciation and recognition, empowering each of us to flourish both individually and collectively. We seek candidates who are inspired by our mission and values, and who are eager to make a meaningful difference on our campus. Learn more about Life at Holy Cross here. The Temporary Academic Records and Registration Coordinator provides critical operational support to the Registrar's Office during the implementation of a new Student Information System (SIS). This two-year, full-time position serves as backfill for existing staff members who are participating in the implementation project or assuming additional project-related responsibilities. The incumbent will support academic records, transfer credit evaluation, study abroad processing, course management, registration activities, and consortium enrollment processes. The position requires strong attention to detail, excellent organizational skills, and the ability to interpret and apply academic policies and procedures. Job Description Primary Job Responsibilities Study Abroad and Transfer Credit Processing Review documentation for students who have completed coursework through approved study abroad programs. Evaluate foreign transcripts and convert approved grades to institutional equivalent grades in accordance with established policies. Record approved study abroad coursework and grades in the student information system. Create course records as needed to facilitate the posting of approved transfer and study abroad credit. Schedule and assign approved courses to student records following departmental and faculty review.   Consortium Enrollment Administration Coordinate enrollment processes for students participating in the Worcester Consortium. Process registrations for Holy Cross students taking courses at consortium institutions. Facilitate enrollment and registration of consortium students attending Holy Cross courses. Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with consortium policies and procedures. Communicate with partner institutions regarding registration, enrollment status, and academic records.   Winter and Summer Course Approval Review requests from students seeking approval to take winter or summer courses at other institutions. Verify institutional accreditation and eligibility for transfer credit consideration. Evaluate proposed coursework to ensure it meets minimum contact-hour requirements and aligns with liberal arts curriculum standards. Process approvals and maintain appropriate documentation of decisions. Communicate requirements, decisions, and follow-up information to students and academic departments.   Academic Records and Registration Support Maintain accurate student academic records and ensure data integrity. Assist with course creation, scheduling, and registration-related processes. Respond to inquiries from students, faculty, and staff regarding registration, transfer credit, study abroad coursework, and academic records. Prepare reports and documentation as requested. Support other Registrar's Office operations as needed to ensure continuity of services during the SIS implementation project.   Support for Assistant Registrar of Curriculum Assist with creating the semester final exam schedule. Assist with proofing of semester schedules prior to the schedule being released. Assist with adding and updating reserved seats for courses.   Workday Implementation Support Assist with end to end testing of student services. Assist with training students on enrollment and other student functions of Workday.   Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated administrative experience in higher education, academic records, registration, student services, or a related field. Strong attention to detail and ability to accurately manage complex records and data. Excellent organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and database or student information systems. Ability to interpret and apply academic policies and procedures while maintaining confidentiality.   Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a Registrar's Office or academic administration environment. Knowledge of transfer credit evaluation, study abroad programs, and student records management. Experience with student information systems and data-entry processes. Additional Information: This position works closely with the Registrar's Office staff, academic departments, and other offices across the college.   This is a full-time, temporary two-year position designed to support continuity of operations during the implementation of a new Student Information System. The position works closely with Registrar's Office staff, academic departments, students, faculty, and external partner institutions. The hourly range for this position is $27.00 $32.00/hour. Weekly Hours: 40 Annual Work Schedule: 52 week (For Seasonal and Temporary Positions, this will be determined by the manager) Application Instructions For all administrative and academic positions, please upload a current resume and cover letter. In your cover letter, please reflect on how your professional and personal values align with the Mission of the College. For all other positions, resume and cover letters are optional, but your most up-to-date work experience and educational background are required. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, priority consideration will be given to applications submitted within 30 days of the posting date. Additional Information To review our generous benefits options, please review our detailed information here or check out our Benefits at a Glance . The College also provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities during the hiring process in compliance with law. Please contact Human Resources for questions or to request an accommodation via email at hr@holycross.edu, or by calling 508-793-3391.  The College is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and complies with all Federal and Massachusetts laws concerning Equal Opportunity in the workplace."
    },
    "https://holycross.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester-MA/Temporary-Administrative-Assistant--JDPC-and-ASLR_JREQ-000656": {
      "title": "Temporary Administrative Assistant, JDPC and ASLR",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Holy Cross, we are focused on creating a world-class workforce by attracting and retaining employees dedicated to fostering a culture of professionalism, pride, mutual trust, and respect—one that values appreciation and recognition, empowering each of us to flourish both individually and collectively. We seek candidates who are inspired by our mission and values, and who are eager to make a meaningful difference on our campus. Learn more about Life at Holy Cross here. Reporting jointly to the Director of Academic Services and Learning Resources (ASLR), and the Director of the J.D. Power Center (JDPC), the Temporary Administrative Assistant provides essential administrative, financial, and operational support across both departments. This role serves as the primary front-facing point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors, while managing program logistics, student employee administration, marketing coordination, travel logistics, and records management. Critically, it assists with coordination of programs (e.g. Passport, The Mentor Program, Tutoring, PAL, Tri-Alpha, and workshops). The position involves extensive, collaborative interaction across campus to ensure the effective delivery of academic support and experiential learning programs. Job Description Major Job Responsibilities  J.D. Power Center Responsibilities and Tasks Assist with  marketing and publicity efforts.Work closely with colleagues to know what events/programs/deadlines they need to publicize. Work with the Washington Semester Program Director to ensure financial aid information is communicated to students. Submit Workday requests and collect relevant information from students to enable processing of financial aid requests. Assist students with completing internship documentation for the Washington Semester Program and Academic Internship Program DC and AIP.  This may include internship application assistance, criminal background checks, documentation of immunizations/medical tests, and/or finalizing contracts/MOUs between Holy Cross and internship sites.  Provide support (i.e., tech support, communications) to the Academic Internship Program faculty as needed.  Make purchases and submit expense reports/pay invoices for J.D. Power Center program as requested- especially the Washington Semester Program, Academic Internship Program, the DC summer program, and grant funding allocated to students and faculty (i.e., Marshall/Ignite Funds). Remain familiar with J.D. Power Center and college policies outlining permissible expenses. Coordinate Uber for Business for students participating in Community-Based Learning, AIP, and the ELPC. Aid students with signing up for Uber for Business, serve as primary liaison with Uber, review and pay invoices. Communicate with students who may not be following Uber-related transportation policies (i.e., overtipping, attending too frequently).   Coordinate van shuttles, transportation, and/or transportation reimbursement for groups associated with/J.D. Power Center. Support the Donelan Office CBL Placement Process by attending the CBL orientation session (8/31 3:30-7), assisting students with signing up for CBL, and delivering paperwork to CBL community partners. Assist with other tasks across the J.D. Power Center as needed including event and meeting planning (i.e., room reservations, ordering food, organization/preparation of printed materials to be distributed). Academic Services & Learning Resources Responsibilities and Tasks  Front Desk, Reception, and General Administrative Support Responsibilities related to serving as a first point of contact, handling routine office operations, and supporting day-to-day administrative needs. Greet visitors and address basic questions; answer phones, and record accurately all messages. Schedule meetings and appointments (using google applications). Monitors departmental email inboxes and ensures timely, accurate responses to inquiries within one business day. Produce and proofread word-processed documents and mail-merges Perform miscellaneous clerical duties in a timely fashion, e.g., collecting and distributing mail, copying, scanning, and filing documents. Manage staff calendars and schedule weekly staff meetings. Record weekly staff meeting minutes. Complete ad hoc projects as requested, by agreed upon deadlines. Ensure that work is done in a timely fashion according to the deadlines of various programs administered by the office; bring overloads to the attention of the department head.   Student Support, Program, and Event Coordination Responsibilities focused on providing operational support for ASLR programming including Passport, PAL, Tutoring, The Mentor Program, English Conversation Club, Tri-Alpha, academic success workshops, academic coaching/advising, and outreach initiatives. Assess each visitor’s needs, determine initial plan and appropriate follow-up by professional staff, and inform all involved parties. Create and maintain accurate registration and participation lists for ASLR summer and fall programming. Work cooperatively with Hogan Conference Services, the Registrar, Facilities, Housing and other campus partners to reserve meetings, workshops, and classrooms well in advance of events. Assists with the promotion and marketing of departmental programs and services through coordinated communications, outreach efforts, and distribution of informational materials. Order appropriate quantities of food through campus dining services or outside vendors. Support program needs including, but not limited to scheduling field trips, arranging transportation (e.g. buses, vans, etc.) ordering textbooks and other program supplies, submitting graphic arts requests, reserving rooms, etc. Request educational technology and audio-visual equipment; follow up with other offices as necessary to ensure events run smoothly.   Student Employee Administration and Payroll Support Responsibilities involving oversight, coordination, and payroll support for student workers across programs. Maintain lists of summer and fall student employees across all ASLR programs Add students to payroll system Observe College policies; help students prioritize their work for various offices and other campus employment Maintain general office supplies; Avoid shortages of critical items while paying attention to budget restrictions.   Minimum Qualifications Bachelors or advanced degree preferred, or a minimum of five years experience in departmental administration and project management. Financial and technical proficiency Confidentiality and discretion Strong communication and collaboration Cross-cultural awareness Initiative and leadership   The hourly range for this position is $24.00 - $26.00 per hour. Weekly Hours: 40 Annual Work Schedule: (For Seasonal and Temporary Positions, this will be determined by the manager) Application Instructions For all administrative and academic positions, please upload a current resume and cover letter. In your cover letter, please reflect on how your professional and personal values align with the Mission of the College. For all other positions, resume and cover letters are optional, but your most up-to-date work experience and educational background are required. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, priority consideration will be given to applications submitted within 30 days of the posting date. Additional Information To review our generous benefits options, please review our detailed information here or check out our Benefits at a Glance . The College also provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities during the hiring process in compliance with law. Please contact Human Resources for questions or to request an accommodation via email at hr@holycross.edu, or by calling 508-793-3391.  The College is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and complies with all Federal and Massachusetts laws concerning Equal Opportunity in the workplace."
    },
    "https://holycross.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester-MA/Music-Lesson-Instructor---Voice_JREQ-000664": {
      "title": "Music Lesson Instructor - Voice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Holy Cross, we are focused on creating a world-class workforce by attracting and retaining employees dedicated to fostering a culture of professionalism, pride, mutual trust, and respect—one that values appreciation and recognition, empowering each of us to flourish both individually and collectively. We seek candidates who are inspired by our mission and values, and who are eager to make a meaningful difference on our campus. Learn more about Life at Holy Cross here. Job Description The College of the Holy Cross seeks a voice instructor to join the Music Department's roster of instrumental and vocal instructors. Lesson instructors are at-will employees and are compensated $1000/semester per student for 10 one-hour lessons and $500/semester per student for 10 one-half-hour lessons. The successful applicant will be required to complete Holy Cross's Boundary Training for lesson instructors. The position reports to the Chair of the music department. Major Areas of Responsibility Teach individual voice lessons, as needed, to music majors and non-majors. Based on the successful candidate's qualification, possible additional ad hoc duties, for which the lesson instructor would receive additional compensation, might include participating in auditions, juries, and coachings.   Minimum Qualifications Master's Degree in Music Performance 3-5 years experience teaching voice lessons to college-age students Experience in professional performance activities Willingness to teach all levels of students from beginning to advanced Willingness to work with ensemble directors in order to help support student participation in ensembles. Evidence of being capable of creating an inspiring and productive teaching environment Willingness and ability to accommodate students' needs of individual learning styles Ability to teach students who enroll in Music 331/332 or 431/432 for a full credit and a letter grade, in coordination with the Chair of the Department Commitment to diversity and inclusion in repertory, for example, music composed by women, historically and geographically underrepresented identity groups, and unfamiliar musics (old and new) Commitment to inclusive excellence in teaching   Preferred Qualifications Evidence of an active performance schedule Interest and/or experience in teaching voice in a liberal arts context Core Competencies Superb musicianship Understands, values, and respects diversity as an individual, in a team, and within groups while fostering an inclusive and supportive environment Good communications skills Dependability This is a part-time opportunity. Lesson instructors are at-will employees and are compensated $1000/semester per student for 10 one-hour lessons and $500/semester per student for 10 one-half-hour lessons. For the first semester only, candidates will be paid for a minimum of three students whether or not three students enroll. Candidates are also eligible, by application and pending budgetary approval, to earn additional income by offering masterclasses, recitals, or serving as ringers in other campus ensembles as needed. All lessons will take place in person, though music lesson instructors are normally able to arrange their lessons into one or two morning/afternoons of teaching per week. Application Instructions:   Electronic applications only. Please submit as a single document with the following application materials (PDF or MSWord) to Holy Cross Employment Opportunities: CV or resume, teaching philosophy statement, links to websites and/or online resources with representative examples of your performances and/or teaching. Two written letters of recommendation may be sent directly to Alice Resker, Academic Department Coordinator: aresker@holycross.edu Please direct any questions to Jessica Waldoff, Chair, Department of Music, College of the Holy Cross: jwaldoff@holycross.edu. Interviews will be conducted remotely. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Weekly Hours: 0 Annual Work Schedule: Application Instructions An updated resume and cover letter are required as a part of your internal application. In your cover letter, please reflect on how your professional and personal values align with the Mission of the College of the Holy Cross to form individuals of integrity and purpose who are committed to the flourishing of all. Additional Information To review our generous benefits options, please review our detailed information here or check out our Benefits at a Glance.  The College also provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities during the hiring process in compliance with law. Please contact Human Resources for questions or to request an accommodation via email at hr@holycross.edu, or by calling 508-793-3391.  The College is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and complies with all Federal and Massachusetts laws concerning Equal Opportunity in the workplace."
    },
    "https://holycross.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester-MA/Culinary-Assistant_JREQ-000639": {
      "title": "Culinary Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Holy Cross, we are focused on creating a world-class workforce by attracting and retaining employees dedicated to fostering a culture of professionalism, pride, mutual trust, and respect—one that values appreciation and recognition, empowering each of us to flourish both individually and collectively. We seek candidates who are inspired by our mission and values, and who are eager to make a meaningful difference on our campus. Learn more about Life at Holy Cross here. Perform various culinary duties to provide meals and services to students and guests following exact menu and recipe specifications with established practices and procedures. Responsibilities include food preparation, cook-to-order line service, station set-up, stocking, rotating product and maintaining a clean safe area following sanitation and food allergy regulations and safety standards. Responsibilities also include the operation of various standard equipment; turbo vector, impinger, deck, rotisserie and convection ovens, slicers, mixers, choppers, flat-top and Panini grills, deep fryers, induction display cooking units, rice/pasta steamers. Other responsibilities include assisting in the set-up, execution and clean-up of catered events and performing other similar tasks as required or requested. Annual certification training required in both ServSafe Food Safety and Food Allergy Awareness. Job Description DAYS & HOURS: Holy Cross Dining staff are considered Emergency Essential Personnel and are required to report during times of inclement weather. Must be flexible.  Schedule may change depending on the needs of the department.   CURRENT SCHEDULE:  Tuesday - Saturday / 9:30 AM - 6:00 PM MAJOR AREAS OF RESPONSIBILITY FOR THIS POSITION Prepare and cook food items to order, ensuring adherence to established standards and specifications. Follow menu and recipe guidelines precisely to maintain consistency and quality across all food items. Ensure all menu items are consistently prepared, properly portioned, of the highest quality, and served at the correct temperatures. Fill out the temperature log book charts. Maintain a clean, safe, and fully functional work area that is adequately stocked, properly rotated, and organized at all times. Supervise on-call staff, student captains/workers, and temporary employees, providing direction on routine tasks to ensure smooth operations. Be adaptable and capable of working in various areas of the servery as assigned by management. Provide exceptional customer service by serving guests in a friendly, professional, and attentive manner when required. Assist with the setup, service, and cleanup of catered events, ensuring all operational standards are met. Accurately complete service records and inventory data within the FoodPro system to ensure proper tracking and reporting. Demonstrate proficiency in accommodating students with special dietary restrictions, ensuring their needs are met with care. Seek guidance from management with questions. Understand and apply food waste management practices, utilizing FIFO (First In, First Out) to minimize waste and maintain inventory efficiency. Adhere to all state and local food safety regulations to ensure compliance and uphold the highest standards of food safety. Perform other similar or related duties as required or requested.     MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR THIS POSITION Up to two years related work experience is preferred. High School Diploma or equivalent required. Ability to frequently lift up to 25 pounds, occasionally lift up to 50 pounds and 100 with assistance ServSafe Food Safety Certification or training is required. If training is not up-to-date, training/certification must be completed upon 3-6 months from date of hire. Food allergy training is essential and prior experience in special food allergy meal preparation is preferred. If a candidate does not have prior experience, the necessary training must be completed upon hiring. Initial training will include a review of information, departmental responsibilities and a recap of the Food Allergy Program. Excellent customer service and appropriate communication skills are needed in order to provide a welcoming, professional and safe environment for students and guests. Upon hiring the following additional training must be completed on a yearly basis: Title IX harassment training, Security awareness training.     RESPONSIBILITIES OF ALL HOSPITALITY EMPLOYEES All documentation is recorded accurately and timely. Follow all chemical guidelines according to the Material Safety Data Sheets. Superior customer service and communications skills are needed to provide a welcoming, friendly and professional manner to all of our guests. Offer training/support to co-workers, staff and students where applicable. Follow all verbal and written instructions from managers/supervisors All staff are considered to be emergency essential personnel and are required to report during times of inclement weather. Schedule flexibility is important, you need to be aware of the academic calendar and special event dates. We will/may adjust schedules due to events on campus. Be innovative as it pertains to your position. Be comfortable sharing your suggestions and ideas for process or work improvements. Comply with all safety and risk management practices, policies and procedures. Ability to perform effectively in a fast-paced food service environment Ability to communicate with guests, co-workers and other members of the college community with professionalism and respect. Be sure to know and come to work each day with our department’s core values in mind. Must adhere to the uniform standard as it applies to your position.   CORE COMPETENCIES Inclusion: Actively engaging with the values of the College by promoting a work environment that embraces diversity and demonstrating respect for the opinions and beliefs of others. Innovation: Performing one’s job with creativity and proactivity, improving procedures and problem-solving. Mission/Service Orientation: Focusing on service to others and contributing to the College’s collective mission. Responsibility: Taking ownership of one’s actions and accountability for one’s tasks and duties. Collaboration: Exchanging information, ideas, and thoughts with others in a manner that is proactive and enhances partnerships.    Salary: The hourly rate for this position is $18.00 per hour.   DISCLAIMER   The description above represents the most significant duties of this position but does not exclude other occasional work assignments not mentioned, the inclusion of which would be in conformity with the factor degrees assigned.   Weekly Hours: 40 Annual Work Schedule: (For Seasonal and Temporary Positions, this will be determined by the manager) Application Instructions For all administrative and academic positions, please upload a current resume and cover letter. In your cover letter, please reflect on how your professional and personal values align with the Mission of the College. For all other positions, resume and cover letters are optional, but your most up-to-date work experience and educational background are required. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, priority consideration will be given to applications submitted within 30 days of the posting date. Additional Information To review our generous benefits options, please review our detailed information here or check out our Benefits at a Glance . The College also provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities during the hiring process in compliance with law. Please contact Human Resources for questions or to request an accommodation via email at hr@holycross.edu, or by calling 508-793-3391.  The College is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and complies with all Federal and Massachusetts laws concerning Equal Opportunity in the workplace."
    },
    "https://holycross.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester-MA/Culinary-Assistant_JREQ-000638": {
      "title": "Culinary Assistant",
